         BEFORE THE NEW MEXICO PUBLIC REGULATION COMMISSION

IN THE MATTER OF THE APPLICATION OF                                 )
EL PASO ELECTRIC COMPANY FOR                                        ) Docket No. 25-00082-UT
REVISION OF ITS RETAIL ELECTRIC RATES                               )
PURSUANT TO ADVICE NOTICE NO. 317                                   )

                      ORDER SETTING SCHEDULING CONFERENCE

        THIS MATTER comes before Keven Gedko and Nicholas Rossi, appointed hearing

examiners, upon the amended filing by El Paso Electric Company for approval of its retail electric

rates pursuant to Advice Notice No. 317. The Hearing Examiners FIND and CONCLUDE that a

scheduling conference should be convened in this matter.

        It is therefore ORDERED:

        A.      A scheduling conference will be held beginning at 10:00 a.m. on Tuesday, August

25, 2026, via the Zoom platform.

        B.      A Zoom invitation including the link to access the prehearing shall be sent to all

parties on the existing service list.

        C. At the scheduling conference all parties should be prepared to discuss a potential

procedural schedule, if additional notice is required, and the treatment of outstanding motions.

ISSUED under the seal of the Commission at Santa Fe, New Mexico, on August 21, 2026.

                          NEW MEICO PUBLIC REGULATION COMMISSION




                          ___________________________
                          Nicholas Rossi
                          Hearing Examiner
                          Nicholas.Rossi@prc.nm.gov
